<div class="markdown-heading" dir="auto"><h2 tabindex="-1" class="heading-element" dir="auto">🔬 Evaluation Pipeline</h2><a id="user-content--evaluation-pipeline" class="anchor" aria-label="Permalink: 🔬 Evaluation Pipeline" href="#-evaluation-pipeline"><svg data-component="Octicon" class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"></path></svg></a></div>
<p dir="auto">The benchmark projects all outputs into consistent visual renderings and structural schemas before evaluation. Content and aesthetic evaluation operate on rendered visual outputs (making scores comparable across template-based, code-driven, and image-centric systems), while editability is measured through format-conditional structural parsing.</p>
<div class="markdown-heading" dir="auto"><h3 tabindex="-1" class="heading-element" dir="auto">📝 Step 1: Content Evaluation (QuizBank)</h3><a id="user-content--step-1-content-evaluation-quizbank" class="anchor" aria-label="Permalink: 📝 Step 1: Content Evaluation (QuizBank)" href="#-step-1-content-evaluation-quizbank"><svg data-component="Octicon" class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"></path></svg></a></div>
<p dir="auto">Content quality is evaluated with a structured VLM-based <strong>QuizBank</strong> protocol, constructed from the source documents themselves rather than a single black-box LLM prompt.</p>
<details><summary>Details</summary>
<b>🧩 QuizBank Construction</b>
<p dir="auto">The QuizBank is built by a three-phase multi-agent pipeline on the source documents:</p>
<ol dir="auto">
<li><strong>Phase I — Drafting:</strong> A <em>Forensic Analyst</em> agent scans the full source document (100k+ tokens) and extracts high-value information into a draft JSON of key points.</li>
<li><strong>Phase II — Critic:</strong> A cyclic feedback loop performs hallucination checks, quote verification, and gap expansion, producing a refined evidence JSON.</li>
<li><strong>Phase III — Exam Setting:</strong> An <em>Exam Setter</em> agent converts the evidence into a standardized probe of exactly <strong>10 MCQs per document</strong> — 5 Concept Questions (high-level understanding) and 5 Data Questions (specific details). All questions are manually verified by the authors.</li>
</ol>
<p align="center" dir="auto">
  <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="/YunqiaoYang/SlidesGen-Bench/blob/main/images/quizbank-pipeline.png"><img src="/YunqiaoYang/SlidesGen-Bench/raw/main/images/quizbank-pipeline.png" alt="QuizBank Construction Pipeline" width="800" style="max-width: 100%;"></a>
</p>
</details>
<details><summary>Details</summary>
<b>📖 QuizBank Evaluation (Open-Book Exam)</b>
<p dir="auto">To decouple visual extraction from semantic comprehension, slides are first parsed into structured Markdown by a VLM; the evaluator VLM then answers QuizBank questions relying <em>solely</em> on this slide-derived context. Accuracy rates serve as a proxy for content quality. A human audit shows that only <strong>1.2%</strong> of errors stem from VLM extraction failures.</p>
<div class="highlight highlight-source-shell notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="# Run content evaluation
python eval/quantitative_eval.py --products Kimi-Standard Kimi-Smart Kimi-Banana NotebookLM Quake Zhipu Gamma Skywork Skywork-Banana --source-mode all --eval-mode content_only --use-grids --workers 4

# Calculate quiz accuracy and generate results
python eval/calculate_quiz_accuracy.py --input results/content_eval.json --quiz-data dataset/slidegen-test.json --output results"><pre><span class="pl-c"><span class="pl-c">#</span> Run content evaluation</span>
python eval/quantitative_eval.py --products Kimi-Standard Kimi-Smart Kimi-Banana NotebookLM Quake Zhipu Gamma Skywork Skywork-Banana --source-mode all --eval-mode content_only --use-grids --workers 4

<span class="pl-c"><span class="pl-c">#</span> Calculate quiz accuracy and generate results</span>
python eval/calculate_quiz_accuracy.py --input results/content_eval.json --quiz-data dataset/slidegen-test.json --output results</pre></div>
</details>
<hr>
<div class="markdown-heading" dir="auto"><h3 tabindex="-1" class="heading-element" dir="auto">🎨 Step 2: Aesthetics Evaluation</h3><a id="user-content--step-2-aesthetics-evaluation" class="anchor" aria-label="Permalink: 🎨 Step 2: Aesthetics Evaluation" href="#-step-2-aesthetics-evaluation"><svg data-component="Octicon" class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"></path></svg></a></div>
<div class="markdown-heading" dir="auto"><h4 tabindex="-1" class="heading-element" dir="auto">📐 Core Aesthetics Metrics</h4><a id="user-content--core-aesthetics-metrics" class="anchor" aria-label="Permalink: 📐 Core Aesthetics Metrics" href="#-core-aesthetics-metrics"><svg data-component="Octicon" class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"></path></svg></a></div>
<p dir="auto">Four computational metrics, grounded in cognitive load theory and visual ergonomics, assess both the <em>spatial quality</em> (single slide) and the <em>temporal coherence</em> (deck pacing):</p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th align="left">Metric</th>
<th align="left">Description</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td align="left"><strong>Harmony</strong></td>
<td align="left">🎨 Fit to harmonic hue templates in HSV space, with a deck-level penalty for cross-slide inconsistency</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td align="left"><strong>Engagement</strong></td>
<td align="left">🌈 Colorfulness via Hasler &amp; Süsstrunk's opponent-channel method, plus a deck-level pacing score</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td align="left"><strong>Usability</strong></td>
<td align="left">🔲 Layout-aware figure-ground contrast within detected text regions (WCAG luminance, logarithmic normalization to the 21:1 ratio)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td align="left"><strong>Visual Rhythm</strong></td>
<td align="left">📊 <strong>VisualHRV</strong>: subband entropy for per-slide clutter combined with RMSSD for temporal variability</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>
<div class="highlight highlight-source-shell notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="python eval/aesthetics_metrics.py IMAGE_PATH [OPTIONS]"><pre>python eval/aesthetics_metrics.py IMAGE_PATH [OPTIONS]</pre></div>
<p dir="auto"><strong>Example Usage:</strong></p>
<div class="highlight highlight-source-shell notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="python eval/quantitative_eval.py --eval-mode aesthetics_only --products Your_product"><pre>python eval/quantitative_eval.py --eval-mode aesthetics_only --products Your_product</pre></div>
<blockquote>
<p dir="auto">📖 For detailed configuration, see <a href="/YunqiaoYang/SlidesGen-Bench/blob/main/docs/Aesthetics_config.md">Aesthetics Configuration Guide</a></p>
</blockquote>
<div class="markdown-heading" dir="auto"><h4 tabindex="-1" class="heading-element" dir="auto">🤖 LLM-as-Judge Methods</h4><a id="user-content--llm-as-judge-methods" class="anchor" aria-label="Permalink: 🤖 LLM-as-Judge Methods" href="#-llm-as-judge-methods"><svg data-component="Octicon" class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"></path></svg></a></div>
<p dir="auto">We also provide LLM-based evaluation methods (used as baselines in the paper):</p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table><table>
<thead>
